2832989,2833388	pát<note n="8" c=" I. Singer has suggested (pers. comm.) that one might want to restore an antonym, e.g. &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;kururiḫḫantes&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt; or &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;idalawantes&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;, which indeed is very enticing. The only reason I have not done so is that I was unable to find these participles used in a similar way in any other text. Cf. &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;kururiḫḫan ḫarta&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt; in KBo 3.4 i 49 and iv 24’ (CTH 61, Annals of Mursili). A writing &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;ku-u-ru-ri-ia-aḫ-ḫa-a&lt;del_fin/&gt;n-te-eš&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt; would seem far too long for l. 28’ here, and KÚR seems not to be used for the participle. Still, the suggestion may well be preferred to the present one."/>
